{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on 92ac92e4 (R14 readiness).\n\n1. Confirmed: the first partial head is a report that compares the catalogue with the recorded sample. It labels each entry observed, not observed, ambiguous or not observable. It reads the operator token from stdin only, and it runs one bounded query of 30 days at most. It adds no instrumentation.\n2. \"Version\" in R14 means the hosted entry points: routes, tools and settings. Use of native platform definition versions is out of the report. The planner answers that from pin readbacks (see e3d5a73e, item 5), not from telemetry.\n3. Retirement is a planner decision on report evidence. The planner runs the query and files each retirement with the label and the sample window. A \"not observed\" entry is evidence, not proof of no use, and the report says so.\n4. Order is unchanged: R14 stays tenth in the security order, after the archive items.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}